        <briefdescription>
<para>Compare <ref refid="structllvm_1_1gsym_1_1_inline_info" kindref="compound">InlineInfo</ref> objects. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>When comparing <ref refid="structllvm_1_1gsym_1_1_inline_info" kindref="compound">InlineInfo</ref> objects the item with the most inline functions wins. If we have two <ref refid="structllvm_1_1gsym_1_1_function_info" kindref="compound">FunctionInfo</ref> objects that both have the same address range and both have valid <ref refid="structllvm_1_1gsym_1_1_inline_info" kindref="compound">InlineInfo</ref> objects, we want the one with the most inline functions to win so we save the most information possible to the GSYM file. We have seen cases where LTO messes up the inline function information for the same address range, so this helps ensure we get the most descriptive information we can for an address range. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
