        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Data</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The binary stream to read the data from. This object must have the data for the <ref refid="structllvm_1_1gsym_1_1_inline_info" kindref="compound">InlineInfo</ref> object starting at offset zero. The data can contain more data than needed.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>BaseAddr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The base address to use when decoding all address ranges. This will be the <ref refid="structllvm_1_1gsym_1_1_function_info" kindref="compound">FunctionInfo</ref>&apos;s start address if this object is directly contained in a <ref refid="structllvm_1_1gsym_1_1_function_info" kindref="compound">FunctionInfo</ref> object, or the start address of the first address range in an <ref refid="structllvm_1_1gsym_1_1_inline_info" kindref="compound">InlineInfo</ref> object of this object is a child of another <ref refid="structllvm_1_1gsym_1_1_inline_info" kindref="compound">InlineInfo</ref> object. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
